    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I see. You mentioned \"perceived threats against Establishment norms.\" To be more precise for my research, can you go into more detail about those norms? Specifically, in some of the more critical sociological literature, is there a discussion about how certain cultural habits or social structures from these specific immigrant groups might be fundamentally at odds with the \"stability\" or \"order\" that the existing communities rely on to function? I want to make sure I'm not glossing over the more contentious arguments regarding social cohesion.",
